From 95b40fc5338ec678eb9fc39216aeb2ddc0dfecd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:51:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] generic-parallel: tests of the isotropic DSLs, of
 ImplicitGenericBehaviour and of ImplicitModel

These DSLs were only compiled for GPUs by the compilation sweeps. The new
test behaviours are compared to the generic interface for all the
configurations:

- IsotropicMisesCreepTest: Norton creep;
- MultipleIsotropicMisesFlowsTest: plasticity with a Voce isotropic
  hardening and Norton creep. This DSL does not provide a consistent
  tangent operator: the generic interface rejects the requests of
  tangent operators, the integrations are compared without them;
- ImplicitGenericBehaviourTest: Norton creep with the strain and the
  stress declared as a gradient and a thermodynamic force;
- ImplicitModelTest: linear ordinary differential equation.
